      "id": 1,
      "text": "Greenfield was incorporated in 1753, breaking away from Deerfield and taking its name from the nearby Green River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greenfield%2C_Massachusetts",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town sits where the Deerfield, Green, and Connecticut rivers meet, a confluence that once powered early trade and industry.",
